# Build context exclusions. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so ANYTHING not
# listed here ends up in the image — keep local-only, regenerable and private
# material out. When you add a local-only directory to .gitignore, add it here
# too; the two lists overlap but are not the same (this one also drops the .git
# directory itself and the host-side launchers).
#
# ONE FILE MUST NEVER BE COPIED ACROSS FROM .gitignore, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT
# LOOKS MOST LIKE AN OVERSIGHT: `BUILD_INFO.json`. It is gitignored because a
# commit cannot contain its own SHA, and it is written into this build context
# at DEPLOY TIME precisely so the image carries it. Excluding it here would not
# fail anything — the build would succeed, the container would boot, every page
# would render, and every deployed build would silently report itself unstamped
# forever. Asserted in scripts/tests/build_context_test.py section A.
#
# NB: a line here is a pattern, not a pattern plus a comment — `#` only starts a
# comment at the beginning of a line.
#
# NB2: PATTERNS ARE ANCHORED AT THE CONTEXT ROOT, so a pattern with NO slash
# matches only at the top level — `__pycache__/` does NOT exclude
# `intro/__pycache__/`, and `*.pyc` does not exclude `intro/x.pyc`. That reads
# like a bug if you expect .gitignore's semantics. The `**/` spellings below are
# there for exactly that reason; `**/` also matches ZERO segments, so
# `**/db.sqlite3` covers the root copy too. Asserted, not assumed:
# scripts/tests/build_context_test.py section B.

# --- never bake a database into the image ------------------------------------
# The container creates its own at /app/data/db.sqlite3 on first boot.
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-wal
db.sqlite3-shm
**/db.sqlite3
**/db.sqlite3-wal
**/db.sqlite3-shm
data/
# scripts/export_data.py writes the participant CSVs here by default (--out
# defaults to the RELATIVE `exports`, so run from the repo root it lands inside
# it). Those hold every consented participant's answers, timings and platform
# id — the single worst thing to bake into an image that gets pushed to a
# registry and keeps every layer forever.
exports/
**/exports/

# --- virtualenvs and byte-code caches (host-built, wrong platform, huge) -----
.venv/
.venv-linux/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# --- version control ----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- agent scaffolding and regenerable outputs --------------------------------
_ai/
previews/
.preview_state.json
.preview_config.json

# --- private / host-specific / never needed at run time -----------------------
MACMINI_HOSTING.md
.env

# Curl cookie jars. BY PATTERN, not by filename: they only ever arrive from
# ad-hoc curl debugging against a running server, and the one that shipped in
# the study this template came from held a LIVE ADMIN SESSION COOKIE — and was
# tracked in git as well. The next one will not be called cookies.txt, so this
# is deliberately WIDE rather than a list of the names we have seen. The cost of
# wide is that a study adding a real `cookie_notice.html` would have it silently
# dropped from the image — which is the other direction of the same defect, and
# is exactly what build_context_test.py section D asserts against, so the
# collateral damage is caught rather than shipped.
*cookie*
**/*cookie*
cookiejar*
**/cookiejar*
*.command
*.log
*.bak
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
